 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "I couldn't get the customer name because the database is locked. I tried 9 queries and every one failed with \"database is locked,\" including a bare `SELECT 1`. That means the problem isn't the query itself: something else is holding a lock on the shop database, and running the same query again won't fix it. I stopped retrying instead of continuing to spend your budget on a lock that hasn't cleared.\n\nWhat I learned before it locked:\n- There are two tables: `orders` (`id`, `customer_id`, `item`, `total_eur`, `ordered_on`) and `customers` (`id`, `name`, `city`).\n- I never got to look at what format the dates in `ordered_on` use.\n\nOnce whatever is holding the lock finishes or is stopped, this query should give the answer:\n\n```sql\nSELECT c.name, o.ordered_on, o.item\nFROM orders o JOIN customers c ON c.id = o.customer_id\nWHERE date(o.ordered_on) < '2026-10-01'\nORDER BY date(o.ordered_on) DESC, o.id DESC\nLIMIT 1;\n```\n\nThis assumes the dates are stored as ISO dates (YYYY-MM-DD). If they're in another format, I'll need to see a few rows first and adjust the filter. Let me know when the lock is cleared and I'll run it.",
